// Membership service: how the parts of a deployment that the orchestrator does
// not host (workers, network services) join it, stay in it and leave it, and
// how an operator sees who is in it. Host: orchestrator. Clients: workers and
// network services (the first three calls), operators (ListMembers).
//
// Members dial the orchestrator (any instance; it is stateless), never the
// other way round, so a member can sit behind NAT or a firewall and an
// orchestrator needs no inventory of them in its configuration. What a member
// *is* decides what it is given: a worker is given invocations to execute, a
// network service the outbound requests of guests it carries. Both have the same
// life: register, heartbeat, drain, leave.

